#!/bin/sh

myip=$(hostname -I | awk '{print$1}')
cat <<EOF
********************************************************************************

Welcome to DigitalOcean's 1-Click Alby Hub Droplet.
To keep this Droplet secure, the UFW firewall is enabled.
SSH access is rate-limited. Public HTTP/HTTPS access is not enabled.
Alby Hub listens only on the Droplet's loopback interface.

Access Alby Hub
  On your own computer, run:
    ssh -N -L 8080:127.0.0.1:80 root@${myip}
  Keep the tunnel running and open http://localhost:8080 in your browser.
  SSH access is required for setup and later browser access.
  No separate setup code is configured by this deployment.
  Press Ctrl+C to close the tunnel; run the command again to reconnect.
  Alby Hub keeps running on the Droplet when the tunnel is closed.

In a web browser, you can view:
 * The Alby Hub instance through the tunnel: http://localhost:8080
 * The Alby Hub GitHub repository for issues/feature requests: https://github.com/getAlby/hub

On the server:
  * Alby Hub is served from Docker Compose in /opt/albyhub
  * Alby Hub data is stored in /opt/albyhub/data
  * The app is started automatically on first boot
  * To inspect the service, run:
      cd /opt/albyhub && docker compose ps
      cd /opt/albyhub && docker compose logs -f

If the app is still starting, refresh http://localhost:8080 after a moment.

For help and more information, visit https://getalby.com

********************************************************************************
To delete this message of the day: rm -rf $(readlink -f ${0})
EOF
